    "display_name": "Mars Rover",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Practice using pandas functions to identify important statistics about fictional environmental conditions on Mars and energy usage by the rover and uncover initial insights.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/4354bed1ebb872a75b387e8699a17fe7-space-car.png",
    "teacher_markdown": "**What Students Should Take Away:**\r\n- Students practice using min() and max() to identify key environmental conditions (e.g., temperature extremes) that impacted the Mars Rover mission.\r\n- Students apply the sum() function to calculate total values (e.g., total battery usage), helping them understand the overall resource consumption.\r\n- Students reinforce their ability to summarize data by applying agg() and groupby(), which allows them to analyze the mission’s performance over time.\r\n\r\n**Misconceptions Students Might Have or Points They Might Struggle With and Tips to Assist:**\r\n- Students might think that only one statistic (e.g., mean) is important, neglecting the significance of other statistics.\r\n  - Tip: Encourage students to consider how each statistic offers a different perspective. For instance, the mean shows overall trends, while min and max highlight extremes.\r\n- Students might treat each variable (e.g., temperature, dust levels) in isolation, without considering how they interact.\r\n  - Tip: Encourage students to think about how different variables might be related. For example, how might dust levels affect solar radiation and battery usage?",
    "name_suffix": "_2026",
